Emulatr: unknown flag: EMULATR_PCTRACE=1

Emulatr -- Alpha AXP / EV6 Architecture Emulator (V4)

Usage: Emulatr --firmware <path> [options]

Required:
  --firmware <path>      raw-binary firmware image to load

Optional:
  --firmware-format <auto|raw|srm>   loader contract (default auto;
                                     auto picks srm on .exe and signature
                                     match, raw otherwise)
  --load-pa  <hex|dec>   physical address to load image at  (default 0x0
                                                            for raw, 0x900000
                                                            for srm)
  --start-pa <hex|dec>   physical address to start at; low bit is PAL bit
                         (default 0x0; ignored in srm format -- entry comes
                         from the descriptor)
  --mem      <bytes>     guest memory size                  (default 64 MiB)
  --max-cycles <N>       cap on the run loop                (default unlimited)
  --autosnapshot <on|off>  periodic auto_*.axpsnap saves      (default on;
                              off = only the named --snapshot-on-pc file is
                              written -- use for cold-boot mint runs to avoid
                              the disk cliff.  Env: EMULATR_AUTOSNAP=off)
  --no-autoload          skip autoload-newest at startup -- forces a genuine
                              cold boot instead of restoring the newest
                              snapshot.  Env: EMULATR_NO_AUTOLOAD=1
  --pal-mode             force palMode = true regardless of start-pa low bit
  --trace    <dec,machine>  DEC listing + machine-parsable trace channels
  --snapshot-on-pc <hex|dec>[,<hex|dec>...]  one-shot snapshot trigger(s);
                              first retire at each PC writes a predig_*.axpsnap.
                              ONE PC: legacy behavior -- also disables auto-save
                              so the file stays mtime-newest for autoload.
                              MULTIPLE PCs (comma-list): each fires once; pair
                              with --autosnapshot off (no auto-save disable) to
                              mint several entry-PC snapshots in one boot.
                              predig_ files are never pruned.
  --snapshot-name-tag <s>  base tag inserted after `predig_` (e.g. gctbuild);
                           multi-PC appends _<pchex> per file.  Default: hex PC
  --inject-interrupt-at-cycle <hex|dec>  EXPERIMENTAL.  Fires a one-shot
                                         synthetic INTERRUPT-class trap (divert
                                         to palBase + 0x100) when cpu.cycleCount
                                         first reaches this value.  Tests the
                                         hypothesis that the sys__cbox MCHK loop
                                         is a deliberate idle wait for an external
                                         IRQ.  Zero = off (default).
  --dump-disasm <pa>:<count>  one-shot disassembly dump fired after firmware
                              load and before run; <count> 4-byte instructions
                              starting at physical address <pa>.  Renders to
                              stderr in the PaDump format (see coreLib/PaDump.h).
                              Requires EMULATR_PA_DUMP=ON at compile time.
  --log-disable <subsys>      silence one subsystem entirely
  --log-only <csv>            silence every subsystem not in the list
  --log-verbose <subsys>      unthrottled emit for one subsystem
  --log-file <subsys>=<path>  redirect one subsystem's emit stream to a file
                              <subsys> is one of: Cbox Unalign IntervalTimer
                              Snapshot PalRelocation ChipsetCsr StepD Misc
                              (case-insensitive).  Requires
                              EMULATR_DIAGNOSTIC_LOGGING=ON at compile time.
  --help                 print this help and exit

On exit:
  0  CPU halted cleanly (CALL_PAL HALT)
  1  any other stop reason (fault, max cycles, parse error)
  2  firmware load failure
